From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_OVN_ONE_CHUNK keeps marks from inside a prompt chunk

ai-engine 083da32bb ported minimally onto the pin stack, not as its 32060d706 era
bundle. Both new modules (cuda_one_chunk.zig, cuda_one_chunk_keep.zig) import only
modules the pin already has, so the surface is: the two files, a `one: ?Capture`
field on Engine and Forward, the enter/leave hooks in prefillChunk, keepAs routing
an inside-chunk mark to keep.keepAt, the NotAtMark test accepting an inside mark,
dumpOnce/moveFlat made pub, and the module export in cuda.zig.

Pin adaptations (the source assumed the later era): Plan.init takes the pin's
`shared` page count (derived from share_pages, as snapshots.keepAs does); the arena
pointer goes through the pin's Arena.ptr() accessor; the local is named `shared` to
avoid the later `held`; ranges() folds row_step to the 128 constant so cuda_forward
stays at the 600-line limit.

Knob off: `one` is null, enter/leave no-op, every launch unchanged. Source receipt
(083da32bb): marks kept from inside a prompt chunk instead of only at its start, with
glm_one_chunk_host.zig as its host check; 7d01784c3 keeps the inner marks (leave reset
the count first).

Gates on pin+0001..0011: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new.
